---
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
import KnowledgeField from '../components/KnowledgeField.astro';
import graph from '../../public/graphs/working/tensor.core.graph.json';
import catalog from '../../public/graphs/working/event-profiles/catalog.json';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../data/seo';

const meta = seo.home;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebSite',
  name: 'TENSOR',
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, '/'),
  description: meta.description,
};
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} hidePageTitle={true} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="section-hero">
    <div class="hero-content container">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <p class="hero-kicker">Cyber investigation / Standard candidate</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title">A common language for <span>investigation.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-definition"><strong>For humans. For agents. Across tools.</strong><br />Connect questions, evidence, and decisions in a record the next investigator can understand.</p>
        <div class="cta-group">
          <Button variant="primary" href="/graphs/?renderer=3d" data-telemetry-event="cta-open-graph" data-telemetry-location="home-hero">Explore the graph <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></Button>
          <Button variant="secondary" href="/core/" data-telemetry-event="cta-open-core" data-telemetry-location="home-hero">Core contract <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></Button>
        </div>
        <p class="candidate-status">OPEN FOR TECHNICAL REVIEW<br /><a href="/review/">Core 0.1.0-draft.1 · Review 2026-10-11.1</a></p>
      </div>
      <KnowledgeField />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="home-register container" aria-label="Working investigation knowledge">
    <p class="register-label">Shared knowledge<br />An open foundation</p>
    <a href="/graphs/"><strong>{graph.nodes.length}</strong><span>Working questions</span></a>
    <a href="/graphs/"><strong>{String(new Set(graph.nodes.map(node => node.category)).size).padStart(2, '0')}</strong><span>Investigation domains</span></a>
    <a href="/graphs/profiles/"><strong>{Object.keys(catalog.profiles).length}</strong><span>Event profiles</span></a>
  </div>

  <section class="home-section container" aria-labelledby="example-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">01 / From evidence to understanding</p>
      <div><h2 id="example-title">An investigation is more than its conclusion.</h2><p>Keep the question, the uncertainty, and the reasoning that brought you here. Then let someone else continue the work.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="investigation-example">
      <div class="example-intro">
        <span class="case-number">INVESTIGATION / AGENT ACTION</span>
        <h3>Did the agent send restricted information?</h3>
        <p>A recorded tool call starts the investigation. It does not answer every question. Follow how new evidence changes an assessment without erasing its history.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/investigation-lab/">Follow the example case <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <ol class="example-trace">
        <li><span class="trace-type">Frame the question</span><p>A specific agent, outbound call, time window, and policy context.</p></li>
        <li><span class="trace-type">Preserve the unknown</span><p>The call is visible; the transmitted content is not yet established.</p></li>
        <li><span class="trace-type">Revise with evidence</span><p>A receipt changes the assessment. The earlier entry and its inputs remain.</p></li>
        <li><span class="trace-type">Make the decision explicit</span><p>Record the selected assessment, rationale, policy, and claimed authority. A decision is distinct from execution.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="section-features" aria-label="What Core preserves">
      <article class="feature-card"><span>01</span><h3>Questions with context</h3><p>Separate a reusable definition from a question about a particular subject and time. Pin the meaning used in each investigation.</p></article>
      <article class="feature-card"><span>02</span><h3>Unknowns and disagreement</h3><p>Distinguish missing evidence from a negative finding. Preserve competing assessments and make selected decisions explicit.</p></article>
      <article class="feature-card"><span>03</span><h3>A history you can hand off</h3><p>Keep evidence references, attribution, original inputs, and revisions together. Declare omissions and unsupported meaning during exchange.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section home-architecture" aria-labelledby="layers-title">
    <div class="container architecture-grid">
      <div class="architecture-copy">
        <p class="section-kicker">02 / Designed to be shared</p>
        <h2 id="layers-title">A public foundation.<br />Room to build.</h2>
        <p>TENSOR defines the investigative meaning beneath vendor tools and business policy. Humans and agents use the same Core.</p>
        <p>No overlay may silently change that meaning. Actor type grants no authority, and imported records do not authorize actions or access to evidence.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/extensions/">Build profiles and extensions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="layer-stack" role="img" aria-label="Human and agent investigators use vendor tools and business policy above public TENSOR profiles and Core. Core connects pinned definitions with portable records.">
        <div class="layer-actors"><span>Human investigators</span><b>+</b><span>Agent investigators</span></div>
        <div class="layer-pair"><div><strong>Vendor layer</strong><small>Tools, integrations,<br />storage, execution</small></div><div><strong>Business layer</strong><small>Policy, authority,<br />thresholds, retention</small></div></div>
        <div class="layer-public"><strong>Public TENSOR profiles</strong><small>Domain questions, vocabulary, evidence requirements</small></div>
        <div class="layer-core"><strong>TENSOR Core</strong><small>Shared investigative meaning<br />Pinned definitions + portable records</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section container" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="section-kicker">03 / Make it useful</p><div><h2 id="start-title">Find your way in.</h2><p>AI security teams are the first adoption community. The scope is all cyber investigations.</p></div></div>
    <div class="home-entry-list">
      <a class="home-entry" href="/investigation-lab/"><span>01</span><h3>Work an investigation</h3><p>Inspect an agent-action or identity case. These authored examples use the same candidate contract for human and agent participation.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="home-entry" href="/implement/"><span>02</span><h3>Build an implementation</h3><p>Use versioned schemas, a documented binding, and a reference CLI. Test which meaning survives the handoff.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="home-entry" href="/graphs/"><span>03</span><h3>Explore the knowledge</h3><p>Navigate every working question and its evidence criteria. The original 588-question release remains separately preserved.</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-review">
    <div class="container">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">04 / A standard in the making</p><h2>Built in the open.<br />Made stronger by scrutiny.</h2></div>
      <div><p>The founding charter, governance proposal, and 38 Core requirements are open for review. TENSOR is designed to work alongside ATT&amp;CK, D3FEND, ATLAS, CASE/UCO, STIX, Attack Flow, CACAO, and OCSF. Mappings require versioned definitions and exchange evidence.</p><div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href="/review/">Review the candidate <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></Button><a class="text-link" href="/standards/">Standards crosswalk <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="review-status">A public implementation candidate.<br />Not a ratified standard or institutional endorsement.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
